diff --git a/docs/glossary.md b/docs/glossary.md
index 04dae4bf40a6c8b701b3a428d2e5bc1d21156684..6e27675c013737ac3a894c667bdf1d8007765bef 100644
--- a/docs/glossary.md
+++ b/docs/glossary.md
@@ -188,7 +188,7 @@ specifies the intended screens; this section names what the code ships.
 | Chat with OpenAgents | Implemented | The chat every new conversation goes to by default, even with a computer ready. It needs no computer or sign-in: each message is a NIP-CJ conversation job the device key signs and NIP-44-encrypts to the chat worker. The assistant speaks as OpenAgents in the plural ("we"), answers from the chat router, and dispatches Coder only when a message needs a computer. It was called the *basic Coder* until 2026-09-28; measurements taken before then keep that name. See [the chat worker](deployment/chat-worker.md) and [the chat router](coder/design/2026-09-28-chat-router.md). |
 | Thread | Defined | One conversation with OpenAgents: what the chat list shows as one entry, on the phone, the desktop, and the `openagents` CLI (`--thread ID`). A thread keeps its turns in order, including the router's answers, knowledge answers, and any Coder work it delegated. Each thread maps to one ATIF trajectory (`ATIF-v1.8`, `session_id` = the thread's ID), so a thread can be exported, replayed, and carried as [NIP-ATIF](../nips/openagents/NIP-ATIF.md). A thread's turns live in `openagents-chat`'s encrypted store (the host's, on a computer), and `openagents_chat::thread` renders any thread as its ATIF document: one step per turn, the router's judgment as a decision call, the served knowledge entry, and a link to Coder work it delegated. `openagents chat export --thread ID` prints it ([#10031](https://github.com/OpenAgentsInc/openagents/issues/10031), [guide](cli/chat.md)). A computer's threads (the desktop's and `openagents chat`'s) reach a paired phone over NIP-HOST `thread.list`, `thread.read`, and `thread.send` ([#10035](https://github.com/OpenAgentsInc/openagents/issues/10035)); the phone lists them beside its own, labelled with the computer, and a follow-up sent there appends to the host's thread. `thread.read` includes the router's offers, cards, and follow-up chips on each turn, inside the same 48 KiB page, dropping the oldest turns' extras first. The typed judgment stays on the host. `thread.run` (`operate`) asks that computer to start Coder for the thread through the host's handoff ([#10040](https://github.com/OpenAgentsInc/openagents/issues/10040)). The code and older notes say *chat* or *conversation* for the same thing. |
 | Chat worker | Implemented | The `coder-worker` binary in quota mode that answers Chat with OpenAgents on `wss://relay.openagents.com`. Its public key is compiled into the app (`basic_coder::WORKER`); it calls `google/gemini-3.8-flash` through the Vercel AI Gateway and asks Jev for the router's judgment beside it. It is open to any key under a quota (6 jobs a minute and 40 a day per key, 3,000 a day in total) and runs under its own release on the Coder worker VM. See [the chat worker](deployment/chat-worker.md). |
-| Coder chat | Implemented | A chat that runs Coder on a connected computer: tapping **Run Coder on** a computer, a chip under a reply the chat router placed on a computer, sends a NIP-HOST `task.create` with the conversation, and the host's auto-start policy runs it. Images attached to the chat's draft go with it as their exact bytes (`artifact.put` chunks, then `task.create` naming them by digest; PNG or JPEG, at most 8 MiB each and 4 a task), and Codex and Claude Code receive them as native image input; the hosted chat itself never carries images ([#10066](https://github.com/OpenAgentsInc/openagents/issues/10066)). On the phone attachments are off as of 2026-10-01: its chat is text only ([#10093](https://github.com/OpenAgentsInc/openagents/issues/10093)). The reply streams into the chat from the task's transcript. The phone lists only chats with OpenAgents and Coder chats; the separate Claude Code, Codex, OpenCode, and Devin history lists and their host mirrors were removed. See [OpenAgents for iOS](../bins/openagents-ios/README.md) and [the chat load benchmark](coder/runtime/chat-load-benchmark.md). |
+| Coder chat | Implemented | A chat that runs Coder on a connected computer: tapping **Run Coder on** a computer, a chip under a reply the chat router placed on a computer, sends a NIP-HOST `task.create` with the conversation, and the host's auto-start policy runs it. Images attached to the chat's draft go with it as their exact bytes (`artifact.put` chunks, then `task.create` naming them by digest; PNG or JPEG, at most 8 MiB each and 4 a task), and Codex and Claude Code receive them as native image input; the hosted chat itself never carries images ([#10066](https://github.com/OpenAgentsInc/openagents/issues/10066)). Attachments are off everywhere as of 2026-10-01: the phone's chat ([#10093](https://github.com/OpenAgentsInc/openagents/issues/10093)) and the desktop's ([#10095](https://github.com/OpenAgentsInc/openagents/issues/10095)) are text only, behind one switch (`coder_tab::ATTACHMENTS_ENABLED`); the image pipeline is kept for when it is turned back on. The reply streams into the chat from the task's transcript. The phone lists only chats with OpenAgents and Coder chats; the separate Claude Code, Codex, OpenCode, and Devin history lists and their host mirrors were removed. See [OpenAgents for iOS](../bins/openagents-ios/README.md) and [the chat load benchmark](coder/runtime/chat-load-benchmark.md). |
 | Delegate session | Implemented | The OpenCode or Devin session a Coder task delegated to on an `opencode` or `devin` route, copied after each turn into the task directory as `<task>.delegate.<agent>.<session>.jsonl` and listed by the Coder catalog as that task's subagent. A device shows it inside the Coder chat, not as a separate chat. See [delegate sessions](../crates/coder-history/README.md#delegate-sessions). |
 | Coder-only host | Implemented | `coder host` serves and watches only a grant's Coder task roots (`Host::coder_only`): an older grant that also names Codex, Claude, OpenCode, or Devin history lists only its Coder chats. The standalone `coder-connect` observer still reads Codex and Claude history for the Coder reader. See [saved harness history](../crates/coder-history/README.md). |
 | Catalog index | Implemented | `coder-history`'s private file of each source's first-record reads (`catalog-index.json` in the host's observer directory), used only while a file keeps the identity and length it was read at, so a restarted host lists chats without reading every source again. See [saved harness history](../crates/coder-history/README.md#read-a-history). |
